Origin: EmberBSD, AI-assisted. Based on the pkgsrc HEAD updates of net/grpc
and net/py-grpcio* to 1.84/1.85.0, moved to the 1.85.1 release.

grpc 1.85.1 fixes the host/:authority handling in the HPACK parser
(grpc/grpc#43797), and in Python a denial of service in the Health Watch RPC
and a memory leak in AsyncIO client-streaming calls with interceptors
(grpc/grpc#43783). Update net/grpc and the py-grpcio packages, which share
the version, to 1.85.1:

- grpc 1.85 builds with OpenSSL 4 on its own (const certificate names and
  extension data, ASN1_STRING accessors), so the local OpenSSL 4 recipe
  patches and their PKGREVISION are no longer needed.
- latent_see.cc uses std::abs upstream; drop the pkgsrc patch for it.
- grpc 1.85 needs the third_party/grpc-proto submodule; fetch the commit
  pinned by the v1.85.1 tag (CMakeLists.txt checks the same sha256).
- libgrpc moves to .so.58 and libgrpc++ to .so.1.85: bump the buildlink ABI
  dependency and the PKGREVISION of sysutils/collectd-grpc, which links
  libgrpc++.
- Follow the setup.py requirements of the 1.85.1 Python distributions.

